Page 7 - ETERNITY

Dan, some lucky person is destined to inherit a fortune left by Barclay Leland Stamford. A parchment was found in the time capsule announcing that the California pioneer has left an extensive will, consisting of ten chapters, detailing his life experiences, knowledge, and advice, and bequeathing more than a billion dollars worth of real estate to the lucky inheritor. There is a possibility, Dan, that the will is lost or misplaced and may never be found. Stamford's announcement stipulates that if no one comes forward with the will within 30 days, or the property is not claimed within 90 days, the property reverts to the State of California. So, we'll just have to wait and see what happens.

INSERT:

Various kinds of calendars (digital, desk, wall, etc.) indicate the passage of the 30 day period, interspersed with newspaper headlines, radio reports, and TV newscasts stating:

SIX PEOPLE CLAIM TO BE STAMFORD'S HEIRS;

GOVERNOR DELANEY APPOINTS COMMITTEE TO EXAMINE THE STAMFORD WILLS;

MORE THAN A HUNDRED WILLS SUBMITTED SO FAR;

STAMFORD WILL COMMITTEE HIRES HANDWRITING ANALYSTS;

836 CLAIMANTS FOR THE STAMFORD FORTUNE;

36 THE FINAL COUNT;

HANDWRITING EXPERTS EXCLUDE 798 WILLS AS BOGUS;

EXPERTS AGREE: 38 WILLS MATCH STAMFORD'S HANDWRITING.

INT. GOVERNOR'S OFFICE - DAY

NEWSPAPER AND TV CORRESPONDENTS gather in the Governor's office to broadcast the ceremony for opening the secondary capsule.
